<section class="section"><div class="container" style="max-width:900px;">

<div style="padding:24px;margin-bottom:24px;border-left:4px solid var(--primary);background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
  <p style="margin:0;font-size:15px;color:var(--text);"><strong>TL;DR:</strong> Expert plasterboard installation for walls and ceilings across Edinburgh. Standard, moisture-resistant, fire-rated, and acoustic options from British Gypsum and Knauf. CSCS-accredited team with 12-month guarantee.</p>
</div>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Plasterboard Installation Services</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Plasterboard is the foundation of modern drylining. At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we provide expert plasterboard installation for walls, ceilings, and custom features in residential, commercial, and industrial properties across Edinburgh and the Lothians. Our team ensures every board is cut precisely, fixed securely, and finished to a professional standard.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Edinburgh's diverse property stock — from Victorian tenements in Newington and Marchmont to modern developments in the Leith Waterfront regeneration zone, historic Georgian properties in Stockbridge and Bruntsfield, and commercial spaces in the New Town — demands skilled plasterboard installers who understand both traditional and contemporary building methods. We work with all fixing methods including direct-to-brick dot and dab, timber stud framing, and metal stud systems, ensuring every installation meets Scottish Building Standards Part H (thermal) and Part C (structural) requirements.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Standard wall and ceiling plasterboard installation</li>
  <li>Moisture-resistant boards for bathrooms and kitchens (Gyproc Showerliner, Knauf MoistureResist)</li>
  <li>Fire-rated plasterboard (30–120 minutes for stairwells, communal areas, and fire compartments)</li>
  <li>Acoustic plasterboard (SoundBloc, Knauf Acoustic) for sound insulation between flats and offices</li>
  <li>Tapered edge and square edge options for different finishing requirements</li>
  <li>Insulated plasterboard (Celotex, Kingspan, Rockwool) for thermal upgrades on solid walls</li>
  <li>Dot and dab direct-to-brick applications — ideal for Edinburgh's solid stone and brick walls</li>
  <li>Timber and metal stud framing for board fixing on new builds and extensions</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Our Plasterboard Installation?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Precision cutting and fitting:</strong> Our team measures and cuts every board with accuracy, ensuring tight joints and a flawless finish around sockets, pipes, and fixtures — critical in Edinburgh's older properties with irregular wall surfaces.</li>
  <li><strong>Minimal disruption:</strong> We work cleanly and efficiently, using dust extraction and protective measures to keep your Edinburgh property tidy throughout the installation, whether it's a home renovation in Morningside or an office fit-out on North Bridge.</li>
  <li><strong>Board expertise:</strong> We help you choose the right board type for each room and application — from moisture-resistant bathrooms to fire-rated corridors in multi-storey buildings and acoustic bedrooms in student HMOs across the city.</li>
  <li><strong>Complete service:</strong> From framing to finishing, we handle every stage including stud work, board fixing, taping, jointing, and final sanding — delivering a paint-ready surface ready for decoration.</li>
  <li><strong>Scottish Building Standards compliance:</strong> Every installation meets current Part H thermal, Part C structural, and Part B fire safety requirements with full documentation provided.</li>
  <li><strong>12-month guarantee:</strong> All our plasterboard installations are backed by a workmanship guarantee for your peace of mind.</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials & Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use industry-leading plasterboard products from trusted UK manufacturers to ensure durability, compliance, and a premium finish on every Edinburgh project.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>British Gypsum Gyproc plasterboard (standard wallboard, Gyproc Showerliner, fire-rated, SoundBloc, Firecode)</li>
  <li>Knauf plasterboard (Platinum, MoistureResist, D34 Fireboard, Acoustic)</li>
  <li>Metal C-studs and U-tracks (50mm, 70mm, 92mm profiles) for stud framing</li>
  <li>Gyproc drywall adhesive for dot and dab applications on brick and block walls</li>
  <li>Joint compound, paper tape, and scrim tape for seamless finishing</li>
  <li>Insulation-backed plasterboard (Celotex XYLI, Kingspan K118, Rockwool MultiPlus)</li>
  <li>Fire-rated intumescent sealants and cavity barriers for fire compartments</li>
  <li>Moisture-resistant boards for wet areas (bathrooms, kitchens, utility rooms)</li>
  <li>Metal corner beads and edge trim for durable corners</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Applications & Use Cases</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our plasterboard installation services are suitable for a wide range of building types and project sizes across Edinburgh and the Lothians.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>New build residential properties and housing estates in the Lothians</li>
  <li>Home renovations, extensions, and loft conversions in Morningside, Bruntsfield, Marchmont, and Portobello</li>
  <li>Commercial office fit-outs and refurbishments in the New Town, Stockbridge, and St Andrew Square</li>
  <li>Retail shop fitting and display wall construction on Princes Street and St James Centre</li>
  <li>School and education building upgrades across Edinburgh Council areas</li>
  <li>Healthcare and care home interior works for NHS Lothian and private healthcare providers</li>
  <li>Industrial unit partitioning and warehouse linings in Leith and Portobello</li>
  <li>Student accommodation and HMO conversions throughout the Edinburgh city centre</li>
</ul>

<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">How It Works</h2>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Free Quote:</strong> Call or fill in our form. We will assess your project, recommend the best board types for your property, and provide a detailed, no-obligation quote.</li>
  <li><strong>Detailed Plan:</strong> We confirm board types, fixing methods, insulation requirements, and timeline. No hidden extras — everything is agreed upfront with full Scottish Building Standards compliance documentation.</li>
  <li><strong>Professional Installation:</strong> Our CSCS-registered team measures, cuts, and fixes boards with precision, working cleanly and efficiently with minimal disruption to your Edinburgh property.</li>
  <li><strong>Quality Check & Handover:</strong> We inspect every joint and surface, ensure compliance with all building standards, and leave your space ready for decoration with full documentation.</li>
</ol>

