<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Frequently Asked Questions about Plasterboard Installation</h2>
<div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What is plasterboard installation?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Plasterboard installation is the process of measuring, cutting, and fixing plasterboard sheets to walls and ceilings. It forms the foundation of drylining and provides a smooth surface ready for decoration.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">How long does plasterboard installation take in Edinburgh?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">A single room takes 1-2 days. Whole-house installations typically take 3-7 days depending on the number of rooms and any complex features like ceilings or bulkheads.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What types of plasterboard do you install in Edinburgh?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">We install standard wallboard, moisture-resistant boards for bathrooms and kitchens, fire-rated boards for safety compliance, acoustic boards for sound insulation, and insulated plasterboard for thermal efficiency.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Do I need plastering after plasterboard installation?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Not necessarily. We offer taping and jointing as an alternative to wet plastering, which produces a smooth, paint-ready finish without the mess and drying time of traditional plaster.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Can plasterboard be installed on existing brick walls?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">Yes. We use the dot and dab method or timber battens to fix plasterboard directly to brick and block walls, creating a smooth surface and improving insulation — ideal for Edinburgh's solid stone and brick properties.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">Is plasterboard installation messy?</h3>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--text-light);margin:0;">We work cleanly and efficiently, keeping dust and debris to a minimum. Our team uses dust extraction equipment and protects floors and furnishings throughout the installation.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="padding:20px;margin-bottom:12px;background:var(--white);border-radius:var(--radius);border:1px solid var(--border);">
    <h3 style="font-size:16px;margin-bottom:8px;color:var(--primary);">What areas do you cover for plasterboard installation in Edinburgh?</h3>
